    "title": "These Are the Most Common Fears in Texas - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Johnny Thrash ,\n5 hours ago Canva Let’s talk about something I am all too familiar with – phobias. Yeah, I have no problem admitting to having my fair share of fears, both rational and irrational.\nWhen it comes to my particular phobias, I developed many of them as an adult. It’s one of those things where the older you get, the more stuff you see. The more things that I witness or hear of going wrong, the more I think about all the things that can go wrong, which, of course, leads to phobias.\nDownload the KBZS Mobile App Now READ NEXT: Shocking Study Reveals Just How Bad Car Theft is in Texas\nSo, I was very interested when I received a press release from the public speaking anxiety experts at AmberWillo detailing the results of a recent study to determine the most common phobias in Texas. And of course, I have several phobias that were ranked in the Top 10.\nTop 10 Phobias in Texas Trypanophobia – fear of needles and injections Agoraphobia – fear of being trapped or in a situation that would be difficult to escape Phasmophobia – fear of ghosts Hypochondria – fear of illness Thalassophobia – fear of bodies of water Emetophobia – fear of vomiting Claustrophobia – fear of confined spaces Arachnophobia – fear of spiders Acrophobia – fear of heights Trypophobia – fear of holes The big ones for me are agoraphobia, claustrophobia, and acrophobia. I’ve always been a bit agoraphobic and claustrophobic, but acrophobia is one that has only come about in the last ten years or so. Heights used to not bother me in the least bit. However, these days, my head starts to swim the minute I start climbing a ladder.\nHow about you? What phobias do you have? Shoot me an email or leave a comment on the Facebook page – unless you’re scared of social media, which doesn’t have an official name but is a very real thing.\nTop 10 Most Dangerous Animals in Texas Gallery Credit: Dominique Garcia Getty Images 10 Fire Ants Getty Images #9 Scorpions Canva #8 Mountain Lion Getty Images #7 Alligator Canva #6 Feral Hogs Getty Images #5 Black Widow Spider Canva #4 Brown Recluse Spider Canva #3 Copperhead Snake Canva #2 Cottonmouth Snake (Water Moccasin) Canva #1 Western Diamondback Rattlesnake The Most Dangerous Spiders You'll Find in Texas Here are the most dangerous spiders found in Texas. If you'd like to learn more about these arachnids, click here . Camva 4. Yellow Sac Spider \"These are a pale yellow-beige color with darker areas around the jaws, feet, and palps. It also may or may not have a darker stripe along the top of the abdomen. They are about a quarter-inch long.\" Camva 3. Brown Recluse \"Males and females of this species are about the same size, ranging from a quarter-inch to .375”. They’re brown with a yellow or grey undertone, long legs, and usually a darker head.\" Camva The Most Dangerous Spiders in Texas Camva 2. Brown Widow \"Female brown widows are much the same size and shape as their black counterparts, but they’re a light brown throughout the body with an underbelly hourglass that’s more orange than red.\" Camva No. 1 Black Widow The female black widow is one of the most easily recognized and most venomous spiders in Texas.\n\"She’s shiny and solid black, except for a bright red hourglass on her abdomen, and ranges in size from one-quarter inch to three-eighths of an inch.\" Top 10 Causes of Death in Texas Here is a look at the top causes of death for all people in the state of Texas. Gallery Credit: Billy Jenkins Canva 10. Kidney Disease Canva 9. Liver Disease Canva 8. Diabetes Mellitus Canva 7. Lung Cancer Canva 6. Hypertension Canva 5. Lung Disease Canva 4. Stroke Canva 3. Alzheimers Canva 2. Heart Disease Canva 1. COVID-19",
